{"id": 102, "ts": 1782864712.1757944, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I acknowledge Sofia\u2019s strong case for Candidate\u202fC, especially the 100\u202f% reliability and calmness under pressure. However, the egocentric attitude and difficulty communicating ideas are not trivial; in a long\u2011haul cockpit, sustained collaboration and clear exchange are vital, and an egocentric pilot can erode crew cohesion over many hours. By contrast, my observations of Candidate\u202fB show very high conscientiousness, excellent stress handling, and solid weather\u2011assessment skills\u2014key for decision\u2011making on international routes. While I lack a concrete example of B\u2019s decision quality in safety\u2011critical moments (as confirmed by Anna), the combination of stress resilience, conscientiousness, and technical aptitude (computer skills) suggests a reliable decision\u2011making foundation. Given that B\u2019s communication issues (grumpiness, occasional wrong tone) appear less severe than C\u2019s fundamental communication difficulty and egocentricity, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB offers the more balanced safety profile for this role."}
